# NOTE: a '#' only starts a comment at column 0; every rule is on its own line.

# --- Go build outputs / test artifacts ---
/dist/
*.test
*.out
*.prof

# --- Differential-gate scratch (fixture + decrypted outputs; regenerated each run) ---
/.difftmp/
# --- Real-backup differential scratch (operator-local; real decrypted data) ---
/.realtmp/

# --- Real-backup material: NEVER committed (personal data; ladder rung 4 is env-driven) ---
# The real-backup differential test reads a path from an env var; nothing local is tracked.
/local
# NO TRAILING SLASH, and that is the whole of it: `/local/` matches a DIRECTORY only, and
# the private layer is normally linked in as a SYMLINK, which git treats as a file. The
# slash-terminated form ignored a real directory and silently tracked the link — caught one
# amend before a push to a public repo.
/testdata/real/

# --- Claude Code machine-local settings ---
/.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
# macOS AppleDouble sidecars (leak into tar/zip; never want them tracked).
._*
